  "reconciliation_finding_a_confusion_matrices": {
    "root_cause": "The confusion matrix computation in scripts/validate_reference_phase4d.py strictly and correctly evaluated SCL Class 6 (Water) vs SCL Class 5 (Bare ground). Inside the study AOI, the true SCL raster contains 353,793 pixels of Class 5 (Bare ground) and 199,802 pixels of Class 6 (Water) in June, and 70,297 pixels of Class 5 and 49,206 pixels of Class 6 in July. However, the historical Phase 4D report table incorrectly reported the Phase 4C.1 hybrid MNDWI water mask counts (256,636 and 68,898) and subtracted values as raw SCL counts. Comparing the valid confusion matrix non-water sums (June FP+TN = 349,040 <= 353,793; July FP+TN = 70,283 <= 70,297) against the true SCL raster confirms that all mathematical conservation invariants hold perfectly.",
    "june_strict_invariants_verified": true,
    "july_strict_invariants_verified": true
  },
