      "mathematical_identity": "99131 = 49206 (SCL 6) + 49899 (SCL 5 with MNDWI>0) + 26 (SCL 4 with MNDWI>0)",
      "exact_match": true
    },
    "scientific_explanation": "In Phase 4C.1, ref_water_mask was constructed via a hybrid rule: clear_mask & ((mndwi > 0.0) | (scl == 6)). During the July 2024 peak flood crest, 49,899 pixels of SCL Class 5 bare ground were heavily waterlogged/saturated, triggering positive MNDWI values. Consequently, Phase 4C.1 reported 99,131 pixels of water. In Phase 4D, strict optical validation used pure SCL Class 6 (49,206 pixels) to avoid spectral false alarms on damp char sand. The 49,925 pixel difference is mathematically explained by 49,899 wet sand pixels and 26 vegetated pixels with MNDWI > 0."
  },
  "vegetation_sensitivity_interpretation": "All evaluated SCL Class 4 pixels (9,813 in June; 30,215 in July) received a candidate non-water prediction from the SAR classifier. Because dense floodplain vegetation and crop canopies are not definitive dry-land references due to radar attenuation and sub-canopy inundation, this result is descriptive of model behavior and does not establish ground-truth classification correctness over vegetated charland.",
  "method_sensitivity_interpretation": "Among the seven evaluated SAR configurations, Lee 5x5 Dual-AND maintains high precision (0.5910 in June; 0.4882 in July) and balanced performance. Unfiltered Dual-AND achieves slightly higher specificity in June (0.8117 vs 0.8041) and lower false positive count (65,728 vs 68,382) at the cost of lower recall (0.4925 vs 0.5141). Dual-OR and 2D Otsu configurations yield higher raw recall (0.8288 and 0.8242 in July) but exhibit increased false alarms over damp soils (specificity 0.3736 and 0.3884). Lee 5x5 Dual-AND remains the scientifically defensible primary configuration.",
